Erik has a good idea. How about the following as well.

A fix for multiple polymorphs is to give objects a probability of polymorphing
when zapped with a wand of polymorph. The probabilities would be adjusted
to tend towards garbage and to eventually become fixed. Each time an object
is zapped with polymorph the probabilitiy of another polymorphing working is 5% less than before or the probability of polymorphing the new object, whichever
is lower. When an object with a 0% probability of polymorphing is zapped 
with polymorph it a) disintegrates, b) explodes, c) becomes a monster,
d) becomes a trap, depending on the object, with a large tendancy to (a) in 
all cases.

Examples:
Object			Probability of polymorphing 
Wand of Wishing		100%	will always become something else
Wand of Polymorph	100%
Wand of Lightning	80%
Wand of Sleep		40%
Wand of Nothing		10%	its hard to make nothing into something
Potion of Poision	50%	polymorph only works half the time
most garbage		10%	after being zapped twice it disintegrates

Example:
Have a wand of Sleep base prob. 40%
Zap with poly. Poly fails(40%) new prob. of poly. is 35%
Zap with poly. Poly succeds(35%) to lightning(80%) new prob. of poly. is 30%
Zap with poly. Poly fails(30%) new prob. of poly. is 25%
Zap with poly. Poly succeds(25%) to nothing(10%) new prob. of poly. is 10%
Zap with poly. Poly fails(10%) new prob. of poly. is 5%
Zap with poly. Poly fails(5%) new prob. of poly. is 0%
Zap with poly. Poly fails(0%) wands may explode if they have charges
		or else they become garbage with prob. of poly. 0%
		lets get garbage i.e. stick or something 0%
Zap with poly. Poly fails(0%) garbage disintegrates (dust).
		very low possibility of poison or sleep trap being created.

Summary:
Used 7 charges to reduce a wand to grabage, but polymorph only succeded twice.

Also each time a wand of polymorphed is zapped it has a power of 3d6(3-18). This
is the number of objects the wand will polymorph subtract one for each object 
successfully polymorphed. Circulate through the list of
objects until a) all have been polymorphed or b) all of the power points have
been used up. While circulating through the list each failure counts as 
a failure as described above (-5% prob. of poly.).

This could make it harder to detect a wand of polymorph. Zap the wand at a small
pile of low value junk. Say 3 objects with 10% prob. of poly. The whole pile
has a good probability of disintegrating. The player may think they have a
wand of teleport away and use it on a monster -- not to good on a low level.

